    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1884">

                <pb facs="1387" n="1271" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.55/69.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul General Snyder to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that under
                    recent legislation, immigrants coming third class or as deck passengers to
                    Panama <pb facs="1388" n="1272" xml:id="pg1272"/> are required to deposit $30
                    with the Government pending presentation of proof that they have obtained
                    permanent work.</p>
                <p>This law was passed, it is claimed, to avoid a possible future menace as a result
                    of the bad financial condition of the country and the number of West Indians and
                    others who have arrived lately and failed to obtain work owing to the completion
                    of the Canal.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alban G. Snyder.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
